#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Tf2/Adding-A-Frame-Cpp.rst:17
msgid ""
"Local coordinate frames make it easier to model sensors, links, joints, and "
"goals in a robot system. This tutorial describes how to add fixed and "
"dynamic frames to a tf2 transformation tree in C++. After following the "
"steps, you will be able to publish extra frames and use them as targets in a "
"turtle demo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Tf2/Adding-A-Frame-Cpp.rst:25
msgid "**Goal:** Learn how to add an extra frame to tf2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Tf2/Adding-A-Frame-Cpp.rst:27
msgid "**Tutorial level:** Intermediate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Tf2/Adding-A-Frame-Cpp.rst:29
msgid "**Time:** 15 minutes"
msgstr ""

